,"w":"light","o":0.3}],"shots":[]}],"audio":{"cards":[{"text":"60 SECONDS","at":{"s":"fact","w":"60"},"d":1.8},{"text":"2 SECONDS","at":{"s":"factProof","w":"2"},"d":1.6},{"text":"3 TO 6 SECONDS","at":{"s":"fix3","w":"3"},"d":1.8}],"sfx":[{"lib":"motor_hum","at":{"s":"fix1","w":"box"},"d":1.4},{"lib":"motor_hum","at":{"s":"how","w":"timer"},"d":1.2},{"lib":"motor_hum","at":{"s":"fix2","w":"feels"},"d":1.2}],"chimes":[{"s":"name"},{"s":"fact","w":"60"},{"s":"name2"},{"s":"fix3","w":"3"},{"s":"congrats"}]},"codeShots":true,"why":"A street corner with a traffic signal on a mast arm over the lane going away and its gray controller box on the sidewalk. The video opens on one red lamp hanging over the road; the full signal and the box come at fix1, then the timer, the lone car at night, the wire loop, the rear-end crash the yellow lamp fixes, and the finished crossing.","hold":true},"sentences":[{"role":"hook","text":"If you hang one red lamp over the road, you have a traffic light."},{"role":"problem","text":"But it never changes, so cars pile up nose to tail at the red."},{"role":"stakes","text":"Drivers wait one minute, then two, then five, and nobody moves."},{"role":"fix1","text":"So you add a green lamp and a gray box that switches them."},{"role":"name","text":"This is a signal controller."},{"role":"how","text":"Inside, a timer switches the lamps from green to red on a fixed clock."},{"role":"fact","text":"One full cycle at a busy corner lasts about 60 to 120 seconds."},{"role":"factProof","text":"Each green lets one car cross the line about every 2 seconds."},{"role":"problem2","text":"But the box runs on a clock, so at midnight one car waits at an empty red."},{"role":"fix2","text":"So you cut a loop of wire into the road that feels a car's metal."},{"role":"name2","text":"This is an inductive loop detector."},{"role":"problem3","text":"But now the light flips the instant a car arrives, and the car behind slams into it."},{"role":"fix3","text":"So you add a yellow lamp that gives drivers about 3 to 6 seconds to stop."},{"role":"fix4","text":"And late at night, quiet corners just flash red, so you stop and go."},{"role":"myth","text":"And the loop under the road is not a scale that weighs your car."},{"role":"mythFact","text":"It feels the metal changing its field, and the box turns the lamp green."},{"role":"finish","text":"Add crosswalk stripes, a stop line, and a street sign."},{"role":"congrats","text":"Congratulations, you have built a traffic light."}]}